    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d412">

                <pb facs="0500" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg388"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.01/77: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the War Trade Board</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">McCormick</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >U.S.S. George Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1919-07-02T16:20:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1919-06-27T15:00:00+04:53"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received July 2, 1919, 4:20
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Have shown your cable<anchor n="18" xml:id="d412-f1"/> to the President. He sees
                    no objection to his [Secretary of War] dealing openly with Kolchak
                    representatives <pb facs="0501" n="389" xml:id="pg389"/> for the purpose of
                    selling supplies, and no objection to proposed financial plan, provided in both
                    cases there is no formal or diplomatic recognition of the Kolchak government in
                    accordance with our former cable. [Navy] 2614.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McCormick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
